# ── Source study material — NEVER COMMIT ──────────────────────────────
# Textbook chapters, lecture decks, and scanned handouts are copyrighted and
# belong to your school or publisher. This is the most important section here.
*.pdf
*.pptx
*.ppt
*.docx

# ── Knowledge Base exports ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Generated by the Knowledge tab's "Export JSON". These contain extracted
# verbatim text from your source material, so they carry the same copyright
# problem as the sources themselves.
LATTE-Knowledge-Base.json
LATTE-Knowledge-Base*.json
kb-*.json

# ── Generated study artifacts ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Derived from copyrighted sources; also just noise in a code repo.
LATTE-Study-View*.md
LATTE-Case-Study*.md
NCLEX-Practice-Questions*.md
NCLEX-Practice-Questions*.txt
NCLEX-Audit-Trail*.md
NCLEX-Audit-Trail*.txt
priority-analysis*.md
priority-analysis*.txt
anki*.txt
*-anki.txt

# ── Secrets ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The suite never writes your API key to disk (it lives in sessionStorage
# only), so nothing here should ever appear. Belt and suspenders.
.env
.env.*
*.key
apikey*.txt

# ── Tooling ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
package-lock.json
npm-debug.log*

# ── OS / editor cruft ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~

# ── Local scratch ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Handy convention: put anything you want kept off GitHub in /local/
local/
scratch/
*.local.*
run-node-*.md
